WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
In one town, one person in a
hundred has a rare condition.

2
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.310
A test for it is ninety per cent accurate:

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.090
positive for ninety per
cent of people who have it,

4
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.930
and negative for ninety
per cent who don't.

5
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.280
You take the test.

6
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.070
It comes back positive.

7
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.180
So is there a ninety per
cent chance you're ill?

8
00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.590
Or does the result change nothing?

9
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.490
In this mission, you'll meet
conditional probability:

10
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.110
the chance of something, given that
something else has already happened.

11
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.100
You'll imagine a round number
of people going through a tree.

12
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.030
These are expected frequencies.

13
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.200
And you'll find conditional probabilities
from two-way tables and Venn diagrams.

14
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.230
Your mission: work out the
chance that you're ill.
